INT. SKY-FERRY GALLEY, ABOVE THE CLOUDSEA - DUSK

Copper pots. Hanging lanterns. A porthole full of pink cloud. The deck tilts gently, then rights itself.

CAPTAIN ZEPHYRA QUILL (40s, salt-and-pepper braid, brass goggles on her forehead) sits at a long table, a ledger open before her. Across from her, FIRST MATE BRANNOCH TAL (30s, scarred cheek, rope-burned palms) peels an apple with a dagger. At the stove, cook PIP SILVERTONGUE (14, flour on her nose) stirs a pot. And at the head of the table, GUNNAR EMBERFIST (60s, dwarf, forge-blackened apron) hammers a loose rivet with a wrench.

ZEPHYRA
Tally's short again.

BRANNOCH
By how much?

ZEPHYRA
Forty crowns.

GUNNAR
Forty crowns buys a lot of rivets.

PIP
Forty crowns buys a lot of pie.

BRANNOCH
Pip, you ate the last of the pie.

PIP
I did not. Gunnar did.

GUNNAR
I did not!

ZEPHYRA
Nobody ate anything. Pie doesn't vanish on its own.

BRANNOCH
It does on this ship.

GUNNAR
Brannoch, hand me that lantern.

BRANNOCH
Hand it yourself, Gunnar.

PIP
I'll get it!

Pip scrambles for the lantern. Gunnar reaches for it too. They collide. The lantern drops, rolls, and stops against the captain's boot. She stoops, retrieves it, and sets it on the table without comment.

ZEPHYRA
Pip, bring the soup. Gunnar, mind the rivet. Brannoch, put the dagger away before you lose a finger.

BRANNOCH
(sheathing it)
Aye, Captain.

PIP
Soup's coming!

GUNNAR
Rivet's holding!

The galley hatch bangs open. A gust of cold air sweeps through. In the doorway stands DAME OSWYTHA MARROWGATE (70s, imperial blue coat, a cane topped with a silver owl). She surveys the room. Silence falls.

OSWYTHA
Captain Quill. A word.

ZEPHYRA
Dame Oswytha. You're a long way from the Admiralty.

OSWYTHA
I came by courier. I had a thing to deliver.

She taps the cane. A small brass tube falls from the owl's beak, rolls across the table, and stops at Zephyra's ledger.

BRANNOCH
(low)
That's the royal seal.

GUNNAR
(lower)
I'll kill the pie thief myself.

PIP
(lowest)
Mother of clouds.

Zephyra breaks the seal. Unrolls the scroll. Reads. Her face does not change, which is worse.

ZEPHYRA
Pardon.

OSWYTHA
Full. Retroactive. For the forty crowns, and the fifteen before that, and the rest.

BRANNOCH
Captain?

ZEPHYRA
We've been pardoned for smuggling.

GUNNAR
Smuggling?

PIP
We smuggled?

ZEPHYRA
Pip, we've always smuggled.

PIP
I thought it was just cargo.

OSWYTHA
It was both.

She turns toward the door. Stops. Looks over her shoulder.

OSWYTHA (CONT'D)
The Admiralty requests that you stop. The Crown, however, would like to hire you.

ZEPHYRA
For what?

OSWYTHA
Smuggling. Of a different sort.

Zephyra laughs, short and surprised. Brannoch whistles. Gunnar sets down the wrench. Pip carries the soup to the table, slowly, eyes wide, and for the first time in her short life says nothing at all.

ZEPHYRA
Dame Oswytha, join us for dinner.

OSWYTHA
I thought you'd never ask.

Chairs scrape. The ship tilts. The lanterns swing.
